# Generic (characteristic-free) generators of the divisor ideal of a point of `Symⁿ C`

`Work.SymQuot.DivOf.charIdeal` is generated by the values `χ_b(b)`, `b ∈ Γ(C,V)`, of the
characteristic polynomials at `b`.  Proving that this is the ideal of the divisor needs, for
each point `w` of the support, a *single* `K`-section `b` separating `w` from the other lift
points and with `ord_w(b - b(w)) = 1`; over a finite `K` that existence is delicate (see
`Submission/Work/NOTES_LEAD_jacobian_divof.md` §1.1).

This file starts the replacement: the generators are the coefficients of the *generic*
characteristic polynomial

`genCharpoly C n V b = ∏_m (T - ∑_i X_i · b_i^(m)) ∈ (MvPolynomial (Fin r) Γ(Cⁿ,Vⁿ))[T]`

for families `b : Fin r → Γ(C,V)`.  Its coefficients are `S_n`-invariant
(`genCharpoly_coeff_coeff_mem`, proved downstream), so a point `φ : A → F` of the chart
evaluates them; the resulting generators of the divisor ideal are the coefficients of

`∏_m (∑_i X_i · (b_i - b_i(x_m)))`,

and the order of that element at a place `w` is `≥` the number of `m` with `x_m = w`, with
equality for a suitable family `b` (a CRT choice over any field, over the *algebraically
closed* extension where the lift lives — no avoidance lemma, no finiteness hypothesis on `K`).
-/
import Submission.Work.SymQuot.DivOf.SymChart

set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.instanceSearchTypes false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

-- Lean v4.35.0-rc3 / Mathlib 5e0c4e5 made `isDefEq` respect transparency when unifying instances; with it,
-- `ZMod.instField` and `ZMod.commRing` (and `Neg (ZMod p)` via `SubtractionMonoid`) no longer unify, which
-- breaks `ring`/`rw`/module-instance search on `ZMod p`. Restore the v4.34 behaviour for this file.


set_option autoImplicit false
set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false

open CategoryTheory Limits AlgebraicGeometry
open scoped Classical

universe u

namespace Work.SymQuot.DivOf

variable {K : Type u} [Field K]

/-- **The generic characteristic polynomial**: `∏_m (T - ∑_i X_i · b_i^(m))`, a polynomial in
`T` with coefficients in `MvPolynomial (Fin r) Γ(Cⁿ, Vⁿ)`. -/
noncomputable def genCharpoly (C : Work.CurveBasics.Curve K) (n : ℕ) (V : C.left.Opens)
    {r : ℕ} (b : Fin r → Γ(C.left, V)) :
    Polynomial (MvPolynomial (Fin r) Γ((prod C.toOver n).left, piOpen C.toOver V n)) :=
  ∏ m : Fin n, (Polynomial.X - Polynomial.C
    (∑ i : Fin r, MvPolynomial.C (coordPullbackAt C n V m (b i)) * MvPolynomial.X i))

end Work.SymQuot.DivOf
